{
	"$schema": "https://mintlify.com/docs.json",
	"theme": "mint",
	"name": "Checkfu",
	"description": "Open-source managed agents for any model. Runs in your own Cloudflare account.",
	"colors": {
		"primary": "#282828",
		"light": "#D6D6D4",
		"dark": "#737373"
	},
	"logo": {
		"light": "/assets/logo-light.svg",
		"dark": "/assets/logo-dark.svg",
		"href": "https://checkfu.com"
	},
	"favicon": "/assets/favicon.svg",
	"appearance": {
		"default": "light",
		"strict": false
	},
	"background": {
		"color": {
			"light": "#FFFFFF",
			"dark": "#171717"
		}
	},
	"styling": {
		"eyebrows": "breadcrumbs",
		"codeblocks": {
			"theme": {
				"light": "github-light",
				"dark": "github-dark"
			}
		}
	},
	"contextual": {
		"options": ["copy", "view", "chatgpt", "claude"]
	},
	"markdown": {
		"schema": true,
		"instructions": [
			"Checkfu is open source (https://github.com/checkfu/checkfu) and runs in the reader's own Cloudflare account. There is no shared hosted base URL: `checkfu deploy` prints the deployment's API URL (`https://<api-worker>.workers.dev` or the CHECKFU_API_DOMAIN hostname, exported as `CHECKFU_BASE_URL` for the CLI, SDK, and curl) and MCP URL (`.../mcp`). Local development serves the API on http://localhost:1337 and MCP on http://localhost:1338/mcp.",
			"Authenticated HTTP requests send the deployment's CHECKFU_API_KEY as `Authorization: Bearer $CHECKFU_API_KEY` (or `x-api-key`) and `Content-Type: application/json` for JSON bodies. Pass `Idempotency-Key` on retriable writes.",
			"Core workflow: create an Agent (`POST /v1/agents`) and an Environment (`POST /v1/environments`), create a Session that references both (`POST /v1/sessions`), send a `user.message` event (`POST /v1/sessions/{session_id}/events`), and follow `GET /v1/sessions/{session_id}/events/stream` until `session.status_idle`.",
			"Other resources: Memory stores (`/v1/memory_stores`), Files (`/v1/files`), Artifacts (`/v1/artifacts`), Vaults and credentials (`/v1/vaults`), Automations (`/v1/automations`), and Webhooks (`/v1/webhooks`). The deployment serves its OpenAPI 3.1 specification at `GET /openapi.json`."
		]
	},
